        "reader_path": "tex/works/doi%3A10.5802%2Fjep.117%40publisher-JEP_2020__7__263_0/reader.pdf",
        "preserved_editorial_scope": "\\paragraph{Editorial problem boundary.}\nProve only Theorem 1.4(2), with its first-obstruction argument retained as necessary core. For a finitely generated group with complex coefficients, a third-order character-algebra deformation at the trivial character forces its first coefficient to be a quadratic form of rank at most two on first homology. This is a necessary obstruction, with no sufficiency or representation-lifting assertion. The coordinate-algebra definitions, trace/augmentation identities, and both complete obstruction arguments are retained. Surrounding statements are context only.\n",
